        "# Correlation Note\n",
        "Nightly price has its strongest relationship with the number of guests a listing accommodates, followed by beds and bedrooms. Review count, review ratings, and availability have very weak individual relationships with price. This suggests that property size is more useful for predicting price than review or availability variables alone."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6x4LG8kayT6T"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 14. Create usable features"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0p4TyDZSym6a"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Extract the numeric bathroom count from text such as \"1.5 baths\".\n",
        "df[\"bathrooms_num\"] = (df[\"bathrooms_text\"].astype(str)\n",
        "                       .str.extract(r\"(\\d+\\.?\\d*)\")[0].astype(float))\n",
        "# Separate numeric columns from categories that need one-hot encoding.\n",
        "numeric_features = [\"accommodates\", \"bathrooms_num\", \"bedrooms\", \"beds\",\n",
        "                    \"minimum_nights\", \"availability_365\", \"number_of_reviews\",\n",
        "                    \"review_scores_rating\", \"reviews_per_month\"]\n",
        "categorical_features = [\"neighbourhood_group_cleansed\", \"room_type\", \"property_type\"]\n",
        "# Combine all model input columns and confirm they exist.\n",
        "features = numeric_features + categorical_features\n",
        "print(\"Missing selected features:\", [c for c in features if c not in df.columns])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "SzIsXdtGymyW",
        "outputId": "024309fa-3ba9-4d8c-cb33-a53be9887cd2"
      },
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Missing selected features: []\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 15. Feature rationale\n",
        "\n",
        "This step keeps features a host can know when setting a price. Capacity,\n",
        "bedrooms, beds, and bathrooms represent listing size; room type and property\n",
        "type represent the space offered; borough represents location; reviews may\n",
        "signal listing quality; and availability/minimum nights describe the host's\n",
        "offering. It intentionally excludes IDs, names, text descriptions, price\n",
        "quotes, and estimated revenue because they either add noise, are difficult to\n",
        "explain, or could leak information related to price."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dzYlmREjymqC"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 16. Train/Test Split\n",
        "This step separates the data into training and testing sets. The models will learn pricing patterns from 80% of the listings in the training set, then make predictions on the remaining 20% of listings in the test set.\n",
        "\n",
        "Keeping the test set separate gives an unbiased way to measure how accurately each model predicts nightly prices for listings it has not seen before."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3vuw_C5pzE-p"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# X contains predictors; y is the nightly-price target.\n",
        "X = df[features].copy()\n",
        "y = df[\"price_num\"].copy()\n",
        "# Hold out 20 percent of listings for an unbiased final evaluation.\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y, test_size=.20, random_state=RANDOM_STATE\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(X_train.shape, X_test.shape)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "pFqXyqLtzEwD",
        "outputId": "406819cb-5089-4474-cb6a-b32685c47c6c"
      },
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "(15369, 12) (3843, 12)\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 17. Build preprocessing"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BWNYyN6SzEjY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Fill missing numeric values and standardize their scale.\n",
        "numeric_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
        "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler())\n",
        "])\n",
        "# Fill missing categories and convert each category into 0/1 columns.\n",
        "categorical_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n",
        "    (\"onehot\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\", sparse_output=False))\n",
        "])\n",
        "# Apply the correct cleaning pipeline to each feature type.\n",
        "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer([\n",
        "    (\"num\", numeric_pipe, numeric_features),\n",
        "    (\"cat\", categorical_pipe, categorical_features)\n",
        "])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SqH5POGdzpfH"
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Data Cleaning Decisions\n",
        "\n",
        "1. We converted the currency-formatted price into a numeric value.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. We removed listings with a missing or zero price, since they cannot be used to train or test a price model.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. We removed the highest 1% of prices (about 2000 dollars and above). A few luxury listings would otherwise dominate the error measure and distort results for typical hosts.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. We filled missing numeric values with the median from the training data.\n",
        "\n",
        "5. We filled missing categories with the most frequent category from the training data.\n",
        "\n",
        "6. We standardized numeric features so that Linear Regression and KNN treat each feature fairly.\n",
        "\n",
        "7. We one-hot encoded borough, room type and property type. This turns categories into numbers without implying that one category is larger or better than another.\n",
        "\n",
        "8. We excluded IDs, listing text, and price-derived or revenue fields. They add noise, are hard to explain, or could leak the answer into the model."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EzRAczzZzug_"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 18. Create a simple benchmark"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "P5OVQ_1v0Pj1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Predict the training-set median price for every test listing.\n",
        "median_prediction = np.repeat(y_train.median(), len(y_test))\n",
        "# Calculate benchmark error; stronger models should improve on this.\n",
        "baseline_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test, median_prediction)\n",
        "baseline_rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, median_prediction))\n",
        "print(\"Baseline MAE:\", round(baseline_mae, 2))\n",
        "print(\"Baseline RMSE:\", round(baseline_rmse, 2))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "cO3pydfS0PE1",
        "outputId": "6f6a2260-cd14-4fee-cc75-3510ed27eb9c"
      },
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Baseline MAE: 168.73\n",
            "Baseline RMSE: 294.14\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 19. Model 1: Linear Regression"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FgoM0tiG0U8m"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Combine the preprocessing steps with an interpretable linear model.\n",
        "linear_model = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"prep\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", LinearRegression())\n",
        "])\n",
        "# Fit only on training data, then predict the untouched test data.\n",
        "linear_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "linear_pred = linear_model.predict(X_test)\n",
        "print(linear_pred[:10])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "DVbjghbc0U1D",
        "outputId": "fdd770f9-b7db-4e51-f054-e51a8eda9701"
      },
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[110.292752   384.57613685  95.51076975 132.81112067  46.51605795\n",
            " 212.61448132 192.89798567 263.25028462  78.11945991  91.76272138]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We combined the preprocessing steps with a Linear Regression model, trained it using the training data, and predicted prices for the test data. The output shows the first 10 predicted Airbnb nightly prices. Linear Regression has no tuning settings, so it was run as is and serves as our simple, interpretable comparison model."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "euvhF1Rb0UdY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 20. Model 2: K-Nearest Neighbors Regression with tuning\n",
        "KNN Regression is the regression version of the nearest-neighbor approach from\n",
        "class. It estimates a listing's price from similar listings. Scaling is\n",
        "important because KNN uses distance between rows."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mjhQZiZp0-xK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Combine preprocessing with a KNN regression model.\n",
        "knn_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"prep\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", KNeighborsRegressor())\n",
        "])\n",
        "# Test nearby-neighbor counts and two distance-weighting choices.\n",
        "knn_grid = {\n",
        "    \"model__n_neighbors\": [5, 10, 20],\n",
        "    \"model__weights\": [\"uniform\", \"distance\"]\n",
        "}\n",
        "# Use 3-fold cross-validation to select the lowest-MAE settings.\n",
        "knn_search = GridSearchCV(knn_pipe, knn_grid, cv=3,\n",
        "                          scoring=\"neg_mean_absolute_error\", n_jobs=-1)\n",
        "knn_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "knn_pred = knn_search.predict(X_test)\n",
        "print(knn_search.best_params_)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "UcIyrGA-0-d6",
        "outputId": "c45d8d7e-652b-40b0-862d-48ba38eb3624"
      },
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'model__n_neighbors': 10, 'model__weights': 'distance'}\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**KNN tuning results.** We tested 3 neighbor counts (5, 10, 20) and 2 weighting options (uniform and distance) using 3-fold cross-validation scored on MAE. The best settings were **n_neighbors = 10** and **weights = distance**, so the 10 most similar listings are used and closer listings count more when estimating a price."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-g_ISRQ5BZzP"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 21. Model 3: Decision Tree Regression with tuning\n",
        "Decision Tree Regression is a course-friendly nonlinear model. It creates\n",
        "easy-to-explain splits, such as separating room type or capacity ranges, but\n",
        "can overfit without limits on tree depth and leaf size."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5211Ogs31a46"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Build a Decision Tree regression pipeline.\n",
        "tree_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"prep\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", DecisionTreeRegressor(random_state=RANDOM_STATE))\n",
        "])\n",
        "# Limit complexity to reduce overfitting.\n",
        "tree_grid = {\n",
        "    \"model__max_depth\": [5, 10, 15],\n",
        "    \"model__min_samples_leaf\": [5, 15, 30]\n",
        "}\n",
        "# Use the same 3-fold MAE process used for KNN.\n",
        "tree_search = GridSearchCV(tree_pipe, tree_grid, cv=3,\n",
        "                           scoring=\"neg_mean_absolute_error\", n_jobs=-1)\n",
        "tree_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "tree_pred = tree_search.predict(X_test)\n",
        "print(tree_search.best_params_)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "PzuQvVLX1atO",
        "outputId": "f09c8821-85e0-4904-ccb6-37d0986cc876"
      },
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'model__max_depth': 10, 'model__min_samples_leaf': 15}\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Decision Tree tuning results.** We limited tree depth (5, 10, 15) and minimum listings per leaf (5, 15, 30) to reduce overfitting, using the same 3-fold cross-validation scored on MAE. The best settings were **max_depth = 10** and **min_samples_leaf = 15**."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "O8dfE7v9Bke2"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 22. Compare every model fairly"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "44lKrPFG1kC1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def regression_metrics(actual, predicted):\n",
        "    # Return three common regression metrics in one consistent format.\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"MAE\": mean_absolute_error(actual, predicted),\n",
        "        \"RMSE\": np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(actual, predicted)),\n",
        "        \"R2\": r2_score(actual, predicted)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "# Put every test-set result in one table for a fair comparison.\n",
        "results = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Linear Regression\": regression_metrics(y_test, linear_pred),\n",
        "    \"KNN Regression\": regression_metrics(y_test, knn_pred),\n",
        "    \"Decision Tree Regression\": regression_metrics(y_test, tree_pred)\n",
        "}).T\n",
        "results.sort_values(\"MAE\")"
      ],
